{
  "about": [
    "The route manifest (spec 011 US1, FR-003/FR-005; plan D3).",
    "",
    "A committed mapping from source-path patterns to the routes those paths",
    "reach, so the review room can say which screens a landing commit touched.",
    "It is honest and dumb on purpose: deriving it from the router is fragile,",
    "and asking the operator each time makes the room useless for the one thing",
    "it exists to do. What keeps it from rotting silently is a pair of committed",
    "tests -- tests/test_route_manifest.py asserts every API route the",
    "application registers is listed here, and web/tests/unit/routeManifest.test.ts",
    "asserts every room path web/src/routes.ts exports is listed here (FR-005).",
    "",
    "Whoever adds a route adds it here in the same diff; whoever adds a source",
    "file that reaches one adds its pattern. A file no pattern matches is never",
    "dropped -- it reads as reaching no known route, which is a fact about the",
    "manifest as much as about the file.",
    "",
    "Patterns are glob-ish: `*` matches inside one path segment, `**` matches",
    "across separators. Every pattern that matches contributes its routes, so",
    "order does not matter. A pattern with an empty route list is a path known",
    "to reach nothing the operator can look at -- a test, a document, a lockfile",
    "-- and that is a different answer from `no pattern matched`."
  ],
  "routes": [
